@startuml seq-04-zero-trust-nrf-oauth2
title Phase 2 — NRF OAuth2 Scoped Tokens (SEC-02): Wrong Scope → 403

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
autonumber

participant "AMF\nfree5gc-amf" as AMF
participant "NRF\nfree5gc-nrf\n(OAuth2 AS)\n:19001" as NRF
participant "SMF\nfree5gc-smf\n:19003" as SMF
participant "UDM\nfree5gc-udm\n:19005" as UDM
participant "Prometheus\n:9090" as Prom

note over NRF : nrfcfg.yaml: oauth: true\nNRF acts as SBI OAuth2 AS (TS 33.501 §13)

== Normal flow: correct scope ==

AMF -> NRF : POST /oauth2/token\ngrant_type=client_credentials\nclient_id=amf\nscope=namf-comm
note right of NRF : AMF is authorized for namf-comm scope
NRF --> AMF : 200 { access_token, scope:"namf-comm", expires_in:3600 }

AMF -> SMF : POST /nsmf-pdusession/v1/sm-contexts\nAuthorization: Bearer <access_token>
SMF -> NRF : POST /oauth2/introspect { token }
NRF --> SMF : 200 { active:true, scope:"namf-comm" }
note right of SMF : scope namf-comm is valid for this endpoint
SMF --> AMF : 201 smContextRef

== SEC-02 Demo: wrong scope ==

AMF -> NRF : POST /oauth2/token\ngrant_type=client_credentials\nclient_id=amf\nscope=nsmf-pdusession
note right of NRF : AMF is NOT authorized for nsmf-pdusession\n(that scope is for SMF→UDM calls)
NRF --> AMF : 403 Forbidden\n{ error:"insufficient_scope" }

note over AMF : Cannot obtain correct token\nSMF call blocked before it starts

AMF -> NRF : POST /oauth2/token\nscope=namf-comm  (correct scope)
NRF --> AMF : 200 { access_token (namf-comm) }
AMF -> SMF : POST /nsmf-pdusession/v1/sm-contexts\nBearer <namf-comm token>
SMF -> NRF : introspect
NRF --> SMF : 200 { active:true, scope:"namf-comm" }
SMF --> AMF : 201 OK

AMF -> Prom : sbi_nrf_token_rejections_total{scope="nsmf-pdusession",nf="amf"} ++
Prom -> Prom : D5 alert: "SBI Token Scope Rejections > 0"

@enduml
